              %g{:style => "fill:rgb(100%,50%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                %use{:x => "699.083729", "xlink:href" => "#FsNWzdYX0dxpO9rYxPRcai7igNs=-glyph0-5", :y => "166.237941"}
              %g{:style => "fill:rgb(100%,50%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                %use{:x => "699.083729", "xlink:href" => "#FsNWzdYX0dxpO9rYxPRcai7igNs=-glyph0-5", :y => "175.17047"}
              %g{:style => "fill:rgb(100%,50%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                %use{:x => "699.083729", "xlink:href" => "#FsNWzdYX0dxpO9rYxPRcai7igNs=-glyph0-5", :y => "184.104244"}
              %g{:style => "fill:rgb(100%,50%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                %use{:x => "699.083729", "xlink:href" => "#FsNWzdYX0dxpO9rYxPRcai7igNs=-glyph0-6", :y => "193.632026"}
          %h3#AsFundamentalGroupOfConfigurationSpace As fundamental group of a configuration space of points
          %p
            Geometrically, one may understand the group of braids in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            (traditionally regarded as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            in this context, though the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
            plays no role in the definition of the braid group as such).
          %p
            (originally due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Hurwitz1891"} Hurwitz 1891, §II
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FadellNeuwirth62"} Fadell &amp; Neuwirth 1962, p. 118
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FoxNeuwirth62"} Fox &amp; Neuwirth 1962, §7
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Birman75"} Birman 1975, §1
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Williams20"} Williams 2020, pp. 9
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong In the plane
          %p We say this in more detail:
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi n
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}^n
            denote the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configurations of n ordered points
            in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuples"} n-tuples
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (z_1, \ldots, z_n)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi i
                  %mo ≠
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z_i \neq z_j
            whenever
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \neq j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fat+diagonal"} fat diagonal
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∖
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Δ
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_n
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\mathbb{C}^n \setminus \mathbf{\Delta}^n_{\mathbb{C}}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} acts
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permuting
            coordinates. Let:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n/S_n
                denote the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
                by this group action, hence the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit"} orbit
                space (the space of
                = succeed "-element" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
                if one likes),
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [z_1, \ldots, z_n]
                denote the image of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (z_1, \ldots, z_n)
                under the quotient
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coprojection"} coprojection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon C_n \to C_n/S_n
                (i.e. its the
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
          %p
            We understand
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = (1, 2, \ldots, n)
            as the basepoint for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [p] = [1, 2, \ldots n]
            as the basepoint for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+unordered+points"} configuration space of unordered points
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n/S_n
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed topological space
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              The
              %em braid group
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
              of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+unordered+points"} configuration space of n unordered points
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Br
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Br(n)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\pi_1
                    \\big(
                    C_n/S_n, [p]
                    \\big)
            %p
              The
              %em pure braid group
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
              of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+ordered+points"} configuration space of n ordered points
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PBr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    PBr(n)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\pi_1
                    \\big(
                    C_n, p
                    \\big)
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            Evidently a braid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            is represented by a path
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: I \to C_n/S_n
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha(0) = [p] = \alpha(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
            projection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi: C_n \to C_n/S_n
            to a path
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{\alpha}
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{\alpha}(0) = p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{\alpha}(1)
            has the same underlying subset as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            but with coordinates permuted:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{\alpha}(1) = (\sigma(1), \sigma(2), \ldots, \sigma(n))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            is exhibited by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            non-intersecting strands, each one connecting an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma(i)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \mapsto \sigma
            appearing as the quotient map of an exact sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi PBr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \to PBr(n) \to Br(n) \to Sym(n) \to 1
          %p
            which is part of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact homotopy sequence
            corresponding to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon C_n \to C_n/S_n
          %p
            %br/
          %p#ForMoreGeneralTopologicalSpaces
            %strong In general surfaces or graphs
          %p
            Since the notion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
            makes sense for points in any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            %a{:href => "#GeometricDefinition"} above
            geometric definition has an immediate generalization:
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            of the (ordered)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            may be regarded as generalized (pure) braid group, called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em surface braid group
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+braid+group"} spherical braid group
            for the case that the surface in question is the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
          %p
            These surface braid groups are of interest in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+topological+field+theory"} 3d topological field theory
            and in particular in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+computation"} topological quantum computation
            where it models
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+anyons"} non-abelian anyons
          %p
            Yet more generally, one may consider the fundamental group of the configuration space of points of any topological space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            For example for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a 1-dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/undirected+graph"} undirected
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
            %em graph braid groups
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#FarleySabalka2009"} Farley &amp; Sabalka 2009
          %blockquote
            %p
              The following should maybe not be here in the Definition-section, but in some Properties- or Examples-section, or maybe in a dedicated entry on
              = succeed ":" do
                %em
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    graph braid groups
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/graph+braid+groups"} ?
          %p
            It has been shown (
            %a{:href => "#AnMaciazek2006"}> An &amp; Maciazek 2006
            , using discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morse+theory"} Morse theory
            and combinatorial analysis of small graphs) that graph braid groups are generated by particular particle moves with the following description:
          %ol
            %li
              %p Star-type generators: exchanges of particle pairs on vertices of the particular graph
            %li
              %p loop type generators: circular moves of a single particle around a simple cycle of the graph
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#BraidGroupsAsMappingClassGroupsOfPuncturedSurfaces Braid groups as mapping class groups of punctured surfaces
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+groups"} braid groups
            are equivalently given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+groups"} mapping class groups
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/punctured"} punctured
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surfaces"} surfaces
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "#Birman69"} Birman 1969
          %h4#AsMappingClassGroupOfAPuncturedDisk For plain braid groups
          %p
            The braid group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br(n)
            may be alternatively described as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
            of a 2-disk
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^2
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            punctures. &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Birman69"}> Birman 1969
            \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            (review includes
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Birman75"} Birman 1975 §4
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#González-Meneses11"} González-Meneses 2011 §1.4
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Massuyeau21"} Massuyeau 2021 §3.3
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Abadie22"} Abadie 2022 §1.3
          %p Concretely, consider
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}
              %p
                denoting the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                distinct points in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+disk"} closed disk
                (with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
                the
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Homeo
                        %mo ∂
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Homeo^{\partial}\big(D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\} \big)
              %p
                denoting the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
                of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} auto
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphisms"} homeomorphisms
                which restrict to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
                under
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Homeo
                        %mi id
                        %mo ∂
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Homeo^{\partial}_id\big(D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\} \big)
              %p
                denoting the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
                which is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
                (which is readily seen to be a
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+subgroup"} normal subgroup
          %p
            Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
            is the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MCG
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi Homeo
                    %mo ∂
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} /
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Homeo
                    %mi id
                    %mo ∂
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  MCG
                  \\big(
                  D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}
                  \\big)
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  Homeo^{\partial}\big(D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\} \big)
                  \\Big/
                  Homeo^{\partial}_{id}\big(D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\} \big)
                  \\,.
          %p Now observe that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                for the case that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
                this group is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+group"} trivial
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander%27s+trick"} Alexander's trick
            %li
              %p
                continuous extension yields an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Homeo
                        %mo ∂
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi ι
                          %mphantom
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mi Homeo
                        %mo ∂
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Homeo^{\partial}\big(D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\} \big)
                      \\xhookrightarrow{\phantom{-}\iota\phantom{-}}
                      Homeo^{\partial}\big(D^2\big)
                      \\,.
          %p
            Combining this implies that for every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi MCG
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\phi] \,\in\, MCG\big(D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}\big)
            there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotopy"} isotopy
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota[\phi] \to id
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/punctures"} punctures
            trace out a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid"} braid
            (in the sense of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop"} loop
            in the symmetrized
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+group"} braid group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MCG
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∼
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  MCG
                  \\big(
                  D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}
                  \\big)
                  \\xrightarrow{\;\;\sim\;\;}
                  Br(n)
                  \\,.
          %p
            and this is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
          #ActionOfBraidGroupOnFundamentalGroupOfPuncturedDisk.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (action of braid group on fundamental group of
                = succeed "-punctured" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %br/
              It follows in particular that the braid group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Br
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br(n)
              has a canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} group action
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
              of the
              = succeed "-punctured" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+group"} free group
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generators
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#AsAutomorphismsOfAFreeGroup"} below
            %p
              See also eg.
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#MargalitWinarski21"} Margalit &amp; Winarski (2021), §7
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#AmramLawrenceVishne12"} Amram, Lawrence &amp; Vishne (2012), §7
          %h4#SurfaceBraidGroupsViaMappingClassGroups For surface braid groups
          %p
            More generally, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            be a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"}> connected
            )
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+of+a+manifold"} boundary
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1, \cdots, x_n \in \Sigma
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interior"} interior
            points.
          %p Then:
          %p
          #SurfaceBraidGroupsAsFibersOfForgettingPuncturesInMCG.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+groups"} mapping class groups
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MCG
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %msup
                      %mi Homeo
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MCG(-) \coloneqq \pi_0 Homeo^{+,\partial}(-)
              )
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi MCG
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MCG(\Sigma)
                  (of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                  itself, presering orientation and the boundary pointwise)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi MCG
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MCG(\Sigma, \{x_1, \cdots, x_n\})
                  (of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                  with “indistinguishable” punctures)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi MCG
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo ,
