                %path{:d => "M -179.561892 -83.601201 L -179.561892 -124.767246 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:miter;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(0.99701,0,0,-0.99701,289.739889,145.62531)"}
                %path{:d => "M -2.484754 2.869285 C -2.034145 1.149274 -1.019356 0.334341 -0.000658257 0.00132794 C -1.019342 -0.335644 -2.034099 -1.146699 -2.488558 -2.870647 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(-0.0000199402,0.99699,0.99699,0.0000199402,110.71352,270.258469)"}
                %path{:d => "M -155.333204 -70.620987 L -26.588914 -70.620987 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:2.79451;stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:miter;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(0.99701,0,0,-0.99701,289.739889,145.62531)"}
                %path{:d => "M -155.333204 -70.620987 L -26.588914 -70.620987 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:1.83812;stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:miter;stroke:rgb(100%,100%,100%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(0.99701,0,0,-0.99701,289.739889,145.62531)"}
                %path{:d => "M -2.360226 -83.601201 L -2.360226 -124.767246 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:miter;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(0.99701,0,0,-0.99701,289.739889,145.62531)"}
                %path{:d => "M -2.484754 2.868401 C -2.034145 1.148389 -1.019356 0.333457 -0.000658239 0.000443564 C -1.019342 -0.336528 -2.034099 -1.147583 -2.488558 -2.867613 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(-0.0000199402,0.99699,0.99699,0.0000199402,287.386277,270.258469)"}
            %p
          %p
            (In this form the statement appears in
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#FarbMargalit12"} Farb &amp; Margalit 2012, Thm. 9.1
          %p
            In words:
            %em
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/punctured"} punctured
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
              of the plain surface by the surface braid group on the set of punctures.
          %p
            For conditions under which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Homeo
                    %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Homeo^{+,\partial}_0(\Sigma) = 1
            see
            %a{:href => "diffeomorphism+group#HomotopyTypeForSurfaces"} here
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
          %p
          #TrivialPi1NecessaryForGeneralizedBirman.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The assumption
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Homeo
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1 \mathrm{Homeo}^{+,\partial}(\Sigma) = 1
              in Cor.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GenBirmanSequenceForTrivialPi"}
              is necessary: Notably the statement fails for all
              = succeed "-punctured" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 2
              (where Cor.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GenBirmanSequenceForTrivialPi"}
              would predict their mapping class groups to be isomorphic to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+braid+groups"} spherical braid groups
              while they are not, see
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "mapping+class+group#MappingClassGroupsOfNPuncturedSpheres"} there
          %h3#AsAutomorphismsOfAFreeGroup As automorphisms of a free group
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+group"} free group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            generators, the MCG-presentation of the braid group (
            %a{:href => "#InTermsOfAutomorphismsOfFreeGroups"}> above
            ) induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
            of the braid group into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+group"} free group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+representation"} faithful
          %p
            This presentation is due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Artin25"} Artin 1925, §6
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#González-Meneses11"} González-Meneses 2011, §1.6
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Bardakov05"} Bardakov 2005, p. 2
          %p
            More in detail, since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of this punctured disk is, evidently, that of the the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circles"} circles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            is is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+group"} free group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_n
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            generators:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_1
                  \\big(
                  D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_ n\}
                  \\big)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\pi_1
                  \\big(
                  \\vee_n S^1
                  \\big)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  F_n
                  \\,.
          %p
            Now the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functoriality
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Grp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1 \,\colon\, Top^{\ast/} \longrightarrow Grp
            implies we have an induced homomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Aut
                  \\big(
                  D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}
                  \\big)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  Aut
                  \\Big(
                  \\pi_1\big(
                  D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}
                  \\big)
                  \\Big)
                  \\,\simeq\,
                  Aut(F_n)
                  \\,.
          %p
            If such an automorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotopy"} isotopic
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(\phi)
            is trivial, which means that the above homomorphism factors through the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
            known as the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MCG
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi Aut
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  MCG
                  \\big(
                  D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}
                  \\big)
                  \\,=\,
                  Aut
                  \\big(
                  D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}
                  \\big)/Aut_0
                  \\big(
                  D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}
                  \\big)
          %p
            Therefore, the above gives a homomorphism of the following form, which turns out to be a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi MCG
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mphantom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo −
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Br(n)
                  \\,=\,
                  MCG
                  \\big(
                  D^2 \setminus \{z_1, \cdots, z_n\}
                  \\big)
                  \\xhookrightarrow{\phantom{--}}
                  Aut(F_n)
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/BraidActingOnFundamentalGroup-Artin1925.jpg", :width => "440px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#Artin25"} Artin 1925
          %p
            Explicitly, the generator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi yb
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} yb_i
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ArtinGenerators"} (1)
            in the Artin presentation(Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ArtinPresentation"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_i
            on the free group on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            generators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_1, \ldots, t_n
            which is given as follows:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "left center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtd
                          %mi j
                          %mo =
                          %mi i
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mi i
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtd
                          %mi j
                          %mo =
                          %mi i
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mi j
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtd
                          %mtext otherwise.
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma_i(t_j)
                  \\,=\,
                  \\left\{
                  \\begin{array}{lcl}
                  t_{i+1} &amp; \vert &amp; j = i
                  \\\
                  t_{i+1}^{-1} \cdot t_i \cdot t_{i+1}
                  \&amp; \vert &amp;
                  j = i + 1
                  \\\
                  t_j &amp;\vert&amp; \text{otherwise.}
                  \\end{array}
                  \\right.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Artin25"}> Artin 1925, (24)
            )
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/BraidActingOnFundamentalGroup-Gonzalez2011.jpg", :width => "540px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#González-Meneses11"} González-Meneses 2011
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_moduli_space_of_monopoles Relation to moduli space of monopoles
          #ModuliSpaceOfkMonopolesStablyWeakHomotopyEquivbalentToClassifyingSpaceOfBraids.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+monopoles"} moduli space of monopoles
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+weak+homotopy+equivalence"} stably weak homotopy equivalent
                to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+group"} braid group
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+weak+homotopy+equivalence"} stable weak homotopy equivalence
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+k+monopoles"} moduli space of k monopoles
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ModuliSpaceOfkInstantons"} (?)
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+group"} braid group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Br
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br({2k})
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 k
              strands:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi Br
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Sigma^\infty \mathcal{M}_k
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\Sigma^\infty Br({2k})
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CohenCohenMannMilgram91"}> Cohen-Cohen-Mann-Milgram 91
            )
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p
            The first few examples of the braid group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br(n)
            for low values of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Br
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
