                Daniel Farley, Lucas Sabalka,
                %em Presentations of Graph Braid Groups
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0907.2730"}> arXiv:0907.2730
                )
            %li
              %p
                Ki Hyoung Ko, Hyo Won Park,
                %em Characteristics of graph braid groups
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1101.2648"}> arXiv:1101.2648
                )
            %li#AnMaciazek2006
              %p
                Byung Hee An, Tomasz Maciazek,
                %em Geometric presentations of braid groups for particles on a graph
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.15256"}> arXiv:2006.15256
                )
          %h3#relation_to_moduli_space_of_monopoles_2 Relation to moduli space of monopoles
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces+of+monopoles"} moduli spaces of monopoles
            related to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+groups"} braid groups
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Cohen"}> Fred Cohen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Cohen"} Ralph Cohen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The topology of rational functions and divisors of surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02398886"} doi:10.1007/BF02398886
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Cohen"}> Ralph Cohen
                , John D. S. Jones
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monopoles, braid groups, and the Dirac operator
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104254240"} euclid:cmp/1104254240
          %div
            %h3#BraidGroupCryptographyReferences Braid group cryptography
            %p
              Partly motivated by the possibility of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computation"} quantum computation
              eventually breaking the security of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cryptography"} cryptography
              based on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"} elliptic curves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+group"} non-abelian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+groups"} braid groups
              for purposes of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cryptography"} cryptography
              (“post-quantum cryptography”).
            %h4#via_conjugacy_search Via Conjugacy Search
            %p
              An early proposal was to use the
              %em Conjugacy Search Problem
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+groups"} braid groups
              as a computationally hard problem for cryptography. This approach, though, was eventually found not to be viable.
            %p Original articles:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Iris Anshel, M. Anshel and D. Goldfeld,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em An algebraic method for public-keycryptography
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.intlpress.com/site/pub/files/_fulltext/journals/mrl/1999/0006/0003/MRL-1999-0006-0003-a003.pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  K.H. Ko, S.J. Lee, J.H. Cheon , J.W. Han, J. Kang, C. Park ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em New Public-Key Cryptosystem Using Braid Groups
                  %em Advances in Cryptology — CRYPTO 2000
                  Lecture Notes in Computer Science, vol 1880. Springer 2000 (
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-44598-6_10"}> doi:10.1007/3-540-44598-6_10
                  )
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Karl Mahlburg,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em An Overview of Braid Group Encryption
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.math.wisc.edu/~boston/mahlburg.pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  Parvez Anandam,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Introduction to Braid Group Cryptography
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://courses.cs.washington.edu/courses/csep590/06wi/finalprojects/anandam.pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  David Garber,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Braid Group Cryptography
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0711.3941"} arXiv:0711.3941
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814291415_0006"} doi:10.1142/9789814291415_0006
              %li
                %p
                  Cryptowiki,
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://cryptowiki.net/index.php?title=Cryptosystems_based_on_braid_groups"} Cryptosystems based on braid groups
            %h4#via_emultiplication Via E-multiplication
            %p
              A followup proposal was to use the problem of
              %em reversing E-multiplication
              in braid groups, thought to remedy the previous problems.
            %p Original article:
            %ul
              %li
                Iris Anshel, Derek Atkins, Dorian Goldfeld and Paul E Gunnells,
                %em WalnutDSA(TM): A Quantum-Resistant Digital Signature Algorithm
                (
                %a{:href => "https://eprint.iacr.org/2017/058"}> eprint:2017/058
                )
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li
                Magnus Ringerud,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em WalnutDSA: Another attempt at braidgroup cryptography
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://ntnuopen.ntnu.no/ntnu-xmlui/bitstream/handle/11250/2622842/no.ntnu%3Ainspera%3A2452886.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y"} pdf
            %p But other problems were found with this approach, rendering it non-viable.
            %p Original article:
            %ul
              %li
                Matvei Kotov, Anton Menshov, Alexander Ushakov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An attack on the Walnut digital signature algorithm
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10623-019-00615-y"} doi:10.1007/s10623-019-00615-y
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li
                José Ignacio Escribano Pablos, María Isabel González Vasco, Misael Enrique Marriaga and Ángel Luis Pérez del Pozo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Cracking of WalnutDSA: A Survey
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Interactions between Group Theory, Symmetry and Cryptology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.3390/sym11091072"} doi:10.3390/sym11091072
            %h4#further_developments Further developments
            %p The basic idea is still felt to be promising:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Xiaoming Chen, Weiqing You, Meng Jiao, Kejun Zhang, Shuang Qing, Zhiqiang Wang,
                  %em A New Cryptosystem Based on Positive Braids
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.04346"}> arXiv:1910.04346
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  Garry P. Dacillo, Ronnel R. Atole,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Braided Ribbon Group
                      = succeed "-based" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mi n
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.solidstatetechnology.us/index.php/JSST/article/view/5573"} JSST:5573
            %p But further attacks are being discussed:
            %ul
              %li
                James Hughes, Allen Tannenbaum,
                %em Length-Based Attacks for Certain Group Based Encryption Rewriting Systems
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/cs/0306032"}> arXiv:cs/0306032
                )
            %p As are further ways around these:
            %ul
              %li
                Xiaoming Chen, Weiqing You, Meng Jiao, Kejun Zhang, Shuang Qing, Zhiqiang Wang,
                %em A New Cryptosystem Based on Positive Braids
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.04346"}> arXiv:1910.04346
                )
